---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Acceptable Use"
  description="Acceptable use requirements for OpenE2EE Relay and OpenE2EE services."
  canonical="/legal/acceptable-use"
>
  <article>
    <header class="article-header">
      <div class="container article-column">
        <a class="back-link" href="/legal">Legal</a>
        <h1>Acceptable Use Policy</h1>
        <p class="lead">Use OpenE2EE services lawfully and without harming people or systems.</p>
        <p class="article-meta"><span>Effective August 26, 2026</span><span>Version 2026-08-26</span></p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="container article-column">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Prohibited activity</h2>
        <p>You may not use OpenE2EE Relay or another OpenE2EE service to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>violate law, sanctions, export controls, or another person’s rights;</li>
          <li>send spam, malware, phishing, abusive automation, or unsolicited bulk traffic;</li>
          <li>exploit, threaten, harass, defraud, or facilitate serious physical harm;</li>
          <li>store or distribute unlawful content, including child sexual abuse material;</li>
          <li>probe, disrupt, overload, bypass, or gain unauthorized access to a service or account;</li>
          <li>hide the origin of prohibited traffic or evade a limit, suspension, or security control; or</li>
          <li>use another customer’s credentials, project, data, or capacity without authorization.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Customer controls</h2>
        <p>
          You must secure project credentials, authenticate users, enforce application access,
          respond to abuse reports, and keep contact information current. Encryption does not remove
          your responsibility for activity that your application enables.
        </p>

        <h2>Enforcement</h2>
        <p>
          OpenE2EE may reject traffic, rate-limit a project, preserve relevant evidence, or suspend
          service when reasonably necessary to stop harm, protect the service, or comply with law.
          Where safe and lawful, we will give notice and a reasonable opportunity to cure. We may
          terminate severe or repeated violations without a cure period.
        </p>

        <h2>Reports</h2>
        <p>
          Report suspected abuse to <a href="mailto:security@open-e2ee.dev">security@open-e2ee.dev</a>.
          Include the affected project or public endpoint, relevant times, and enough detail to
          investigate. Do not send message plaintext or private cryptographic material unless we ask
          for it through a protected channel.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
